AOR FX2 FIRMWARE - PLACEHOLDER
===============================

This directory is where FoxSDR's native AOR digital-I/Q driver
(src/source/aor_source.cpp) looks for AOR's Cypress FX2 firmware:

    resources/firmware/aor/fx2fw.hex

The file is NOT in this repository yet. fx2fw.hex is AOR, Ltd.'s copyrighted
firmware. AOR has said it will supply the file together with its
redistribution notice; when it arrives:

  1. put fx2fw.hex here, byte for byte as AOR supplies it (unmodified), and
  2. replace this NOTICE with AOR's copyright and firmware-licence notice,
     verbatim, and keep it next to the file in every package that ships it
     (installers, AppImage, MSIX, the CI zip).

The firmware is AOR's and is separate from FoxSDR's own code and licence. Per
AOR's developer documentation it may be redistributed unmodified for use with
AOR receivers under AOR's notice, and it is provided AS IS.

Until the file is present, opening an AOR receiver whose I/Q interface has no
firmware running fails with a plain message naming this path, and the
receiver is not opened. A receiver whose firmware is already running (loaded
by other software since it was powered on) does not need the file.
